        <region top="540" color="#000000">
          <area collapsed="true">
            <title lang="eng">
              <content>
                <p>Margin of Safety</p>
              </content>
            </title>
          </area>
          <region left="0" top="558" width="764" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
            <text lang="eng" width="764" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
              <content>
                <p style="font-weight: bold; font-family: Arial;">Margin of Safety tests: Positive values indicate there is no chance of failure during normal operation, negative that failure is possible during normal operation. The Tol check is used if there is a tolerance to the Designed Value, Abs if they are without tolerance.</p>
              </content>
            </text>
          </region>
          <region left="0" top="612" width="618" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
            <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
              <content>
                <p style="font-weight: bold;">Eg. a MoS of 100% means the designed value would need to double before a failure is possible.</p>
              </content>
            </text>
          </region>
          <region left="0" top="648" width="544" height="43" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
            <math>
              <input>
                <e type="operand">DesignedValue</e>
                <e type="operand">Tol</e>
                <e type="operand">FailurePoint</e>
                <e type="function" args="3">MoS.Tol</e>
                <e type="operand">FailurePoint</e>
                <e type="operand">DesignedValue</e>
                <e type="operand">1</e>
                <e type="operand">Tol</e>
                <e type="operator" args="2">-</e>
                <e type="bracket">(</e>
                <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
                <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
                <e type="operand">1</e>
                <e type="operator" args="2">-</e>
                <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
              </input>
            </math>
          </region>
