        <region top="5535" color="#000000">
          <area collapsed="true">
            <title lang="eng">
              <content>
                <p>Solve For Diode Voltage/Current</p>
              </content>
            </title>
          </area>
          <region left="0" top="5553" width="775" height="68" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
            <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
              <content>
                <p style="font-weight: bold;">The function is a template placeholder for you to add your own function (see below) for returning a diode current, given a diode voltage. If/Vf are the rated current/voltage of the diode and are used to reduce the number of iterations required to get to a solution. Is is the the diode reverse bias saturation current. Tj is the junction temperature. N is the ideality factor (2 is used for most diodes).</p>
              </content>
            </text>
          </region>
